			<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 text-sm">
				<div class="bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour rounded-xl p-5">
					<h3 class="font-bold text-mapa-ink mb-2">What are the operating hours of the EDSA Carousel?</h3>
					<p class="text-mapa-ink/80 leading-relaxed text-xs">
						The EDSA Carousel operates <strong>24 hours a day, 7 days a week (24/7)</strong>. Peak daytime services run with high frequency (every 2 to 5 minutes) between 4:00 AM and 11:00 PM, while nighttime service runs at 10 to 15 minute headways between 11:00 PM and 4:00 AM.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour rounded-xl p-5">
					<h3 class="font-bold text-mapa-ink mb-2">How do I board and pay for the EDSA Carousel?</h3>
					<p class="text-mapa-ink/80 leading-relaxed text-xs">
						Passengers access the median busway via dedicated pedestrian footbridges or elevator-equipped concourses (such as One Ayala and PITX). Fare payment is made upon entry at median turnstiles or directly to the bus conductor inside the vehicle. Always prepare small bills or coins.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour rounded-xl p-5">
					<h3 class="font-bold text-mapa-ink mb-2">Who is entitled to the 20% statutory fare discount?</h3>
					<p class="text-mapa-ink/80 leading-relaxed text-xs">
						Under Philippine statutes—Republic Act No. 11314 (Student Fare Discount Act), Republic Act No. 9994 (Expanded Senior Citizens Act), and Republic Act No. 10754 (Persons with Disability Act)—bona fide students, senior citizens, and PWDs are entitled to a mandatory 20% fare discount upon presenting valid IDs.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="bg-mapa-canvas-dark border border-mapa-contour rounded-xl p-5">
					<h3 class="font-bold text-mapa-ink mb-2">How does EDSA Carousel connect to MRT-3 and LRT-1?</h3>
					<p class="text-mapa-ink/80 leading-relaxed text-xs">
						EDSA Carousel links directly with LRT-1 at Monumento, Balintawak, and Roosevelt (FPJ). It shares direct footbridge walkways with MRT-3 at North Avenue, Quezon Avenue, Santolan, Ortigas, Guadalupe, Buendia, and Ayala. At Taft Avenue, it connects to both MRT-3 and LRT-1 EDSA station.
					</p>
